error[E0513]: unexpected `end` at the top level; it does not close anything
  --> 1:1
   |
  1| end
   | ^^^

error[E0515]: a `def` must be at the top level of a script; for a local function, assign a lambda: `name = ->(x) { … }`
  --> 2:3
   |
  2|   def g
   |   ^^^

error[E0515]: `private` is only allowed at the top level of a script
  --> 2:3
   |
  2|   private
   |   ^^^^^^^

error[E0515]: write `private def name …`, or `private` on a line of its own to apply it to the `def`s below it
  --> 1:9
   |
  1| private :helper
   |         ^^^^^^^

error[E0516]: method names ending in `?` are not supported yet; rename `alive?`, for example to `is_alive`
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| def alive?
   |     ^^^^^^

error[E0516]: method names ending in `!` are not supported yet; rename `reset!`, for example to `reset`
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| def reset!
   |     ^^^^^^

error[E0517]: `next` takes no value in Grindlang
  --> 2:8
   |
  2|   next x
   |        ^

error[E0517]: `break` takes no value in Grindlang
  --> 2:9
   |
  2|   break 1
   |         ^

error[E0512]: chained assignment (`a = b = …`) is not supported in Grindlang; assign each on a line of its own
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| a = b = 0
   |       ^

error[E0512]: an assignment can't be used as a value in Grindlang; assign on a line of its own
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| if (x = f()) then end
   |       ^

error[E0512]: cannot assign to this expression; assign to a name, a constant, `@name`, `x.name`, or `x[i]`
  --> 1:1
   |
  1| f() = 1
   | ^^^

error[E0528]: `or` binds more loosely than `=` in Ruby, so the assignment would happen before the `or`; write `||`, or put the right side in parentheses
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| x = a or b
   |       ^^

error[E0528]: `and` binds more loosely than `=` in Ruby, so the assignment would happen before the `and`; write `&&`, or put the right side in parentheses
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| x = a and b
   |       ^^^

error[E0528]: `or` after a call without parentheses would apply to the whole call in Ruby; put the arguments in parentheses: `say(…)`
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| say a or b
   |       ^^

error[E0511]: `not` can't be used here; write `!`, or put the expression in parentheses
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| x = not a
   |     ^^^

error[E0510]: a `{` right after a call opens a block, not a hash; pass a hash in parentheses: `foo({ key: value })`
  --> 1:5
   |
  1| foo { hp: 1 }
   |     ^

error[E0510]: expected `(` or a line break after `def f`, found `x`
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| def f x
   |       ^

error[E0510]: expected `{` or `do` to start the lambda's body, found `x`; put its parameters in parentheses: `->(x) { … }`
  --> 1:7
   |
  1| f = ->x { x }
   |       ^

error[E0510]: `unless` can't have an `elsif`; use `if`
  --> 2:1
   |
  2| elsif b
   | ^^^^^
